Fillets: the intersection at the end of a rounding with a periodic face at
the end whose parametric seam lies at the end vertex, taken in one period
(mitcad#343).

The case: a bore's top rim of radius 82 is rounded with 0.5 where a pocket
of radius 25.5 cuts into it; the rim, an arc from one side of the pocket
round to the other, starts at one of the pocket's sides, and so does its
torus' parametric seam. The pocket's top rim is then rounded with 1 up to
that torus. At the seam end the rounding's contact on the top runs past
the torus' edge, where the torus grows up to the cut: its point on the
torus, from the top's edge with the torus prolonged, came out at u = 6.263,
a period beyond the face's domain [-0.005, 5.692], while the other end,
on the bore's side, lay at u = -0.002 in it. PerformIntersectionAtEnd
walked the intersection of the blend with the torus between the two the
long way round: a curve of 3.3e6 mm whose edge had a tolerance of 2.5e6
and a body of 1e12 mm3 that the checker took for valid. The rim's other
end, away from the seam, was built (its ends in one period).

- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformIntersectionAtEnd: on a periodic face at the end,
  an end of the intersection that lies outside the face's domain, more
  than half a period from the other end, which lies in it, is taken in the
  period next to that other end (in u and in v), before the intersection
  is computed.

On the design's replayed body before the item and on the stored body:
valid, the material taken -7.525 and -7.615 mm3 at the seam end (the other
end's rounding of the same edge -7.618 and -7.512), every face of the
three roundings taken one after the other on the stored body after the
item within 9e-4 mm both ways; before, the result at the seam end was the
1e12 mm3 body. No synthetic body reproduced the end past the face's edge
at the seam.

Upstream: new.
